{
  "version": "18.0.6-rc.2",
  "releaseNotes": "**Release notes**\n* 🐛 Fixed a crash when opening News, Events, Places and other content items after the app received a live update.\n\n**Builder release notes**\n* 🐛 Fixed app preview in the Builder: pop-up messages and confirmation dialogs now appear and work as expected.\n\n**Developer notes**\n* 🐛 Metro now resolves the Shoutem UI, theme and animation packages from a single copy, so bundles built on the build agents no longer end up with duplicated React contexts.\n* 🐛 The startup console error filter no longer throws on non-string errors, which previously turned recoverable errors into fatal crashes and hid the original message.\n* 📦 Added the missing `react-native-web` 0.21.2 patch (Alert implementation and related web fixes) to the platform.\n* 📦 Re-targeted the `@react-native-firebase/app` web patch from 19.2.2 to the installed 21.14.0 so patch-package applies it again.\n* 🧹 Synced platform-level files between the mobile and platform repos: `eslint-plugin-react-hooks` 4.6.2, `@react-native/assets-registry` in the web template, Ruby 3.4 gems in the Gemfile, editor and gitignore config, and the configure scripts (extension dependencies are now hoisted into the root package.json during configure).",
